---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import DocCode from "../../components/docs/DocCode.astro";
import DocCallout from "../../components/docs/DocCallout.astro";

const toc = [
  { title: "Entry Point", href: "#entry-point", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Interactive Workflows", href: "#interactive-workflows", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Services & Remote", href: "#services-remote", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Integration & Automation", href: "#integration-automation", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Models & Config", href: "#models-config", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Maintenance", href: "#maintenance", depth: 2 },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="CLI Reference"
  subtitle="Command surface defined in packages/nikcli/src/index.ts and packages/nikcli/src/cli/cmd."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="entry-point" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Entry Point</h2>
    <p>
      Running <code>nikcli</code> without a subcommand opens the default terminal UI. From the same
      binary you can also boot servers, attach to shared sessions, manage connectors, configure
      models, and control companion or mobile workflows.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash">
      nikcli
    </DocCode>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Default TUI">
      <p>
        The default TUI command is <code>$0 [project]</code> and accepts session, model, agent,
        continue, prompt, and network flags.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="interactive-workflows" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Interactive Workflows</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Command</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli</code></td><td>Open the TUI in the current workspace.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli [project]</code></td><td>Open the TUI in another project directory.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli run [message..]</code></td><td>Run a one-shot prompt without entering the TUI.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli attach &lt;url&gt;</code></td><td>Attach a local TUI to a shared session URL.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli session</code></td><td>List, inspect, export, or import sessions.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli debug</code></td><td>Print environment and runtime diagnostics.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCode language="bash">
      nikcli run "audit this repo and summarize risks"
      nikcli attach https://example.nikcli.store/share/abcd
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="services-remote" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Services & Remote</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Command</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli serve</code></td><td>Start the local HTTP API server.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli web</code></td><td>Start the local web UI.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli companion serve</code></td><td>Boot the server with the companion web UI enabled.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli companion open</code></td><td>Open the companion UI in the browser.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli mobile</code></td><td>Serve pairing, token, and mobile host flows.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli workspace-serve</code></td><td>Expose workspace event streams for remote consumers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli remote</code></td><td>Start, inspect, share, or stop a remote session server.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli acp</code></td><td>Start the ACP server.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli mcp</code></td><td>Start the MCP server.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Remote attach">
      <p>
        The <code>remote</code> command documents server lifecycle and sharing, but
        <code>remote attach</code> is not implemented in the current command surface.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="integration-automation" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Integration & Automation</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Command</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli connectors</code></td><td>Add, list, auth, or revoke service connectors.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli bot</code></td><td>Manage chat bots for Slack, Discord, Teams, Google Chat, Linear, and GitHub.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli plugin &lt;module&gt;</code></td><td>Install and merge a plugin module into config.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli github</code></td><td>Install GitHub app integrations and helpers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli pr [number]</code></td><td>Inspect a pull request inside the CLI.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli lovable build</code></td><td>Open a Lovable build flow from the terminal.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="models-config" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Models & Config</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Command</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli auth</code></td><td>Manage provider credentials.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli models [provider]</code></td><td>Inspect or refresh the model catalog.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli agent</code></td><td>Inspect or update agent defaults.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli rag-model</code></td><td>List or set the embedding provider and model for RAG.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli image-model</code></td><td>List or set the default image generation provider and model.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>nikcli speak-model</code></td><td>List or set the default text-to-speech provider and voice.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="maintenance" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Maintenance</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>generate</code></td><td>Generate OpenAPI and related assets.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>stats</code></td><td>Inspect usage and runtime statistics.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>export [sessionID]</code></td><td>Export session data as JSON.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>import &lt;file|url&gt;</code></td><td>Import session data from file or share URL.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>upgrade [target]</code></td><td>Upgrade to the latest or a specific version.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>uninstall</code></td><td>Remove nikcli with optional keep-config, keep-data, dry-run, and force flags.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
